--
 -- This File describes SciTEProject.lua, parsectags.lua and AutocompleteNew.lua 
--

Years ago i used SciTE alot that days on my older Win7 machine because of its small size and pure efficient plain win32 Api use.
But its cpp apis sucked, its autocomplete feature was limited and so i had a wild thought:
live CTAGS based Syntax Highlightening and a better Autocomplete for SciTE would be a good Idea.


-- SciteProject.lua (projectHome detection, scite.session.api and .properties generation, apply syntax Highlitening)

Since CTAGS needs to know where it has to search for files, and which options to use there, i used SciteDirectory.properties for that task.
When one opens a File in SciTE,  SciteDirectory.properties in that or a parent folder above the opened File is parsed.
Also SciTE always knows the path to SciteDirectory.properties and such - you know the path to the projects root.
So i wrote SciTEProject.lua to make use of that Scenario and read some vars in - named:
[project.name], [file.patterns.project],  [project.ctag.languages] and [project.ctags.opt] .

Those are used to spawn Ctags and "parsectags.lua" in an OnSave Event as an asynchronous process.
spawner.dll has been modified to run with lower privs for this to not disturb scite while doing so.
As a result, scite.session.properties and scite.session.api are created in the CTAGS Folder besides sciteDirectory.properties. 
After finishing them, it creates "tmp\scite.project.fin" to notify SciteProject.lua that its ready.

A second event, namely onDwellStart, is then used to periopdically check for the fun file and apply the generated syntax highlightening Data.
props used for that are:
 ["colour.project.class"] ["colour.project.functions"] ["colour.project.constants"] ["colour.project.modules"] ["colour.project.enums"]
 Thats all. SciTEProject.lua should be called early with luas dofile() in scitestartup.lua to register its handlers.
 
Note: Only more recent SciTEs understand scite.readproperties so live updating syntax highlitening is only supported there.
Note2: only the cpp lexer is supported for this, as it supports substyles.
Note3: it has been extensively tested with Scintilla, Lexilla and SciTE in the same Projectroot but dont try to use it for Bigger projects.

Finally, all you have to do is edit and  place sciteDirectory.props to a projects root, load a file in there and press save.
A sample has been provides in the tools folder.

-- parsectags.lua

i needed to convert the ctags file to scites proprietary formats. and it shoulb be fast. But i didnt have any c skills. so i wrote it in lua
and rewrote it recently using a lot of grammars. i dont like writing grammars so i used deepseek to do that for me and teach me about taming those digital ants.
It turned out the little "machine god" really shined on that task and so the whole parser was ready shortly without cryptic hassle.  

-- AutocompleteNew.lua

Back then, i also used Fincs Autocomplete.lua. It enhanced SciTEs to also autocomplete current buffers tokens, which is a great thing to have,
Having the the data ready i extended it to automatically include ac_{lexername}.api in ["APIDir"] and ["SciTEDirectory.properties"]\ctags\scite.session.api 
The reason for that was that SciTEs is really flat and shows anything in Brackets behind a functions name in the calltip so you cannot include
additional meta data on entries. But if you dont include it in scites apipath and parse it manually, you are nearly set.

eg in a future time the api file could include the filename it was defined in, such supporting a "jump to definition" feature.
a first idea of a more structured file format would use |as a delimiter and wellknown names for features. eg |fDesc for a Description.
-> acos(double x):double|fDesc Compute arc cosine (function)[c90 c99 arm cpp98 cpp11]|fHeader [<cmath> (math.h)]|filename ...

Again, some grammars were utilized to support class::method like autocompletition where one could type either one to get autocompletition.
Calltips were straight forward and display only function definitions, not including stuff after it.
Note: for some reason, using autocomplete for the very first time after load introduces a short delay.
This has chance of roughly 1 to 5 to happen on my old dev machine.

-- static api files 
ac.cpp.api and mingw.functions. api contain the cpp std:: namespace (up to cpp14) and most functions from mingw headers for inclusion in scites apipath.
 
my dev machine is an old 2018 Notebook and using all above caused no problems.
Developing all that was done in little chunks over a really long time period.
Its nice to see the design functional but implementing this as lua dll would be premium if your interested in.

Have anice Day. arjunae@nurfuerspam.de
